    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, plus all generated sources compiling cleanly) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a read-only `selfLink` field to the owner resource, returned as `/api/owners/` + the owner's id.\n\nTwo edits, following the existing derived-field conventions in this repo:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` property to the `Owner` schema (`readOnly`, string), so the OpenAPI generator produces the getter/setter on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto` plus a `formatSelfLink` method that returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (null when the owner/id is absent), mirroring the other MapStruct-derived fields like `displayName` and `contactPreference`.\n\nBecause `getOwner` (and `addOwner`) map through `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, the field is populated automatically on both create and read. The acceptance test `coreReturnsSelfLink` and the full test suite pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
